.TH sudo 1
.SH NAME
sudo \- execute a command as superuser
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sudo
.I command
.RI [ args " ...]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Sudo
executes
.I command
with the privileges of the superuser (root).  It is intended for users who
are permitted to administer the system but do not run every session as
root.
.PP
The caller must be a member of the
.B wheel
group, as listed in
.BR /etc/group .
If the caller is already root,
.B sudo
executes
.I command
directly without further checks.
.PP
If the root account has no password, privileges are assumed immediately.
Otherwise
.B sudo
prompts for the root password and verifies it against the hash stored in
.BR /etc/passwd .
The command is then executed with a real and effective user id of zero.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP 15
.BI command " " [ args "...]"
The command to execute, with optional arguments.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.I 0
.I Command
executed successfully.
.TP
.I 1
An error occurred: usage error, the caller is not in the
.B wheel
group, no root entry exists in
.BR /etc/passwd ,
an incorrect password was supplied, or
.I command
could not be found.
.SH FILES
.PD 0
.TP
.B /etc/passwd
User database, consulted for the root entry and password hash.
.TP
.B /etc/group
Group database, consulted for
.B wheel
group membership.
.PD
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR passwd (1),
.BR login (1).
